The <computeroutput>has_value</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when an instance of <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> exposes a <computeroutput>value</computeroutput> member. It is used to detect framework value-wrapper types such as <computeroutput>integral_constant</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>floating_point_constant</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>value&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput>, enabling specialised comparison and reporting. </para>
